{"strongs": "H8492", "word": "תִּירוֺשׁ", "translit": "ti.rosh", "root": "ירק", "morph": "H:N-M", "pos": "noun masculine", "gloss": "must, fresh or new wine", "definition": "תִּירוֺשׁ noun masculine Judg 9:13 must, fresh or new wine ; ** on meaning, see ARSK Ency. Bib. WINE (iv. 5307 f.) . — absolute תִּירוֺשׁ Num 18:12 + 24 t.; תִּירשׁ Gen 27:28 + 3 t.; suffix תִּירוֺשִׁי Judg 9:13 ; Hos 2:11 תִּירשְׁךָ Deut 7:13 + 4 t. Deuteronomy; תִּירוֺשֵׁךְ Isa 62:8 תִּירוֺשָׁם Ps 4:8 — must, new wine , as enlivening הַמְּשַׂמֵּחַ אֱלֹהִים וַאֲנָשִׁים ׳ ת Judg 9:13 as injurious יִקַּחלֵֿב ׳ זְנוּת וְיַיִן וְת Hos 4:11 in poetry regarded as contained in the grapes יִמָּצֵא בָּאֶשְׁכּוֺל ׳ הַתּ Isa 65:8 , compare Isa 24:7 (|| גֶּפֶן ); as yielding wine ( יַיִן ), וְלֹא תִּשְׁתֶּה יָ֑יִן ׳ תִּדְרֹךְ זַיִת וְלֹא תָסוּךְ שֶׁמֶן וְת Mic 6:15 usually as a sign of fertility, or as valuable product: יְקָבֶיךָ יִפְדֹ֑צוּ ׳ וְת Prov 3:10 with must thy vats shall burst open ; + דָּגָן (q. v.) Gen 27:28 ; Gen 27:37 (both J ) Hos 2:11 ; Hos 7:14 ; Ps 4:8 ; Isa 62:8 ׳ ת Hos 9:2 (|| גֹּרֶן , יֶקֶב compare דָּגָן v Hos 9:1 ); ׳ וְת ׳ אֶרֶץ ד Deut 33:28 + יִצְהָר Joel 2:24 ; Neh 10:38 (+ פְּרִי כָלעֵֿץ ); + דָּגָן and יִצְהָר Hos 2:10 ; Hos 3:24 ; Deut 7:13 ; Deut 11:14 ; Deut 12:17 ; Deut 14:23 ; Deut 18:4 ; Deut 28:51 ; Jer 31:12 ; Hag 1:11 ; Joel 1:10 ; Joel 2:19 ; 2Chr 32:28 ; Neh 5:11 ; Neh 10:40 ; Neh 13:5 ; Neh 13:12 ׳ חֵלֶב ת Num 18:12 (see ׳ ח ; + id. ); ׳ ת 2Chr 31:5 + דגן , יצהר , and דְּבַשׁ ; אֶרֶץ לֶחֶם וּכְרָמִים ׳ אֶרֶץ דָּגָן וְת Isa 36:17 = 2Kgs 18:32 ( + ארץ זית יצהר ודבשׁ ).", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB3768')\">BDB3768</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H8492')\">H8492</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB3767')\">BDB3767</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB3769')\">BDB3769</entry></div><p> <bdbheb>תִּירוֺשׁ</bdbheb> <b>noun masculine</b><sup><ref ref=\"Judg 9:13\" b=\"7\" cBegin=\"9\" vBegin=\"13\" cEnd=\"9\" vEnd=\"13\" onclick=\"bcv(7,9,13)\">Judg 9:13</ref></sup> <highlightword>must, fresh or new wine</highlightword>; <div class=\"remarks\"><b>**</b>on meaning, see ARSK<sup>Ency. Bib. WINE (iv. 5307 f.)</sup>. — absolute <bdbheb>תִּירוֺשׁ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Num 18:12\" b=\"4\" cBegin=\"18\" vBegin=\"12\" cEnd=\"18\" vEnd=\"12\" onclick=\"bcv(4,18,12)\">Num 18:12</ref> + 24 t.; <bdbheb>תִּירשׁ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Gen 27:28\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"27\" vBegin=\"28\" cEnd=\"27\" vEnd=\"28\" onclick=\"bcv(1,27,28)\">Gen 27:28</ref> + 3 t.; suffix <bdbheb>תִּירוֺשִׁי</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Judg 9:13\" b=\"7\" cBegin=\"9\" vBegin=\"13\" cEnd=\"9\" vEnd=\"13\" onclick=\"bcv(7,9,13)\">Judg 9:13</ref>; <ref ref=\"Hos 2:11\" b=\"28\" cBegin=\"2\" vBegin=\"11\" cEnd=\"2\" vEnd=\"11\" onclick=\"bcv(28,2,11)\">Hos 2:11</ref> <bdbheb>תִּירשְׁךָ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Deut 7:13\" b=\"5\" cBegin=\"7\" vBegin=\"13\" cEnd=\"7\" vEnd=\"13\" onclick=\"bcv(5,7,13)\">Deut 7:13</ref> + 4 t. Deuteronomy; <bdbheb>תִּירוֺשֵׁךְ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Isa 62:8\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"62\" vBegin=\"8\" cEnd=\"62\" vEnd=\"8\" onclick=\"bcv(23,62,8)\">Isa 62:8</ref> <bdbheb>תִּירוֺשָׁם</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Ps 4:8\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"4\" vBegin=\"8\" cEnd=\"4\" vEnd=\"8\" onclick=\"bcv(19,4,8)\">Ps 4:8</ref> — <highlight>must, new wine</highlight>, as enlivening <bdbheb>הַמְּשַׂמֵּחַ אֱלֹהִים וַאֲנָשִׁים</bdbheb> <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>ת</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Judg 9:13\" b=\"7\" cBegin=\"9\" vBegin=\"13\" cEnd=\"9\" vEnd=\"13\" onclick=\"bcv(7,9,13)\">Judg 9:13</ref> as injurious <bdbheb>יִקַּחלֵֿב</bdbheb> <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>זְנוּת וְיַיִן וְת</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Hos 4:11\" b=\"28\" cBegin=\"4\" vBegin=\"11\" cEnd=\"4\" vEnd=\"11\" onclick=\"bcv(28,4,11)\">Hos 4:11</ref> in poetry regarded as contained in the grapes <bdbheb>יִמָּצֵא</bdbheb> <bdbheb>בָּאֶשְׁכּוֺל</bdbheb> <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>הַתּ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Isa 65:8\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"65\" vBegin=\"8\" cEnd=\"65\" vEnd=\"8\" onclick=\"bcv(23,65,8)\">Isa 65:8</ref>, compare <ref ref=\"Isa 24:7\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"24\" vBegin=\"7\" cEnd=\"24\" vEnd=\"7\" onclick=\"bcv(23,24,7)\">Isa 24:7</ref> (|| <bdbheb>גֶּפֶן</bdbheb>); as yielding wine (<bdbheb>יַיִן</bdbheb>), <bdbheb>וְלֹא תִּשְׁתֶּה יָ֑יִן</bdbheb> <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>תִּדְרֹךְ זַיִת וְלֹא תָסוּךְ שֶׁמֶן וְת</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Mic 6:15\" b=\"33\" cBegin=\"6\" vBegin=\"15\" cEnd=\"6\" vEnd=\"15\" onclick=\"bcv(33,6,15)\">Mic 6:15</ref> usually as a sign of fertility, or as valuable product: <bdbheb>יְקָבֶיךָ יִפְדֹ֑צוּ</bdbheb> <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>וְת</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Prov 3:10\" b=\"20\" cBegin=\"3\" vBegin=\"10\" cEnd=\"3\" vEnd=\"10\" onclick=\"bcv(20,3,10)\">Prov 3:10</ref> <highlight>with must thy vats shall burst open</highlight>; +  <bdbheb><reflink>דָּגָן</reflink></bdbheb> (q. v.) <ref ref=\"Gen 27:28\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"27\" vBegin=\"28\" cEnd=\"27\" vEnd=\"28\" onclick=\"bcv(1,27,28)\">Gen 27:28</ref>; <ref ref=\"Gen 27:37\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"27\" vBegin=\"37\" cEnd=\"27\" vEnd=\"37\" onclick=\"bcv(1,27,37)\">Gen 27:37</ref> (both <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('J')\"><reflink>J</reflink></lookup>) <ref ref=\"Hos 2:11\" b=\"28\" cBegin=\"2\" vBegin=\"11\" cEnd=\"2\" vEnd=\"11\" onclick=\"bcv(28,2,11)\">Hos 2:11</ref>; <ref ref=\"Hos 7:14\" b=\"28\" cBegin=\"7\" vBegin=\"14\" cEnd=\"7\" vEnd=\"14\" onclick=\"bcv(28,7,14)\">Hos 7:14</ref>; <checkingNeeded/><wrongReferenceRemoved/> <ref ref=\"Ps 4:8\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"4\" vBegin=\"8\" cEnd=\"4\" vEnd=\"8\" onclick=\"bcv(19,4,8)\">Ps 4:8</ref>; <ref ref=\"Isa 62:8\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"62\" vBegin=\"8\" cEnd=\"62\" vEnd=\"8\" onclick=\"bcv(23,62,8)\">Isa 62:8</ref> <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>ת</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Hos 9:2\" b=\"28\" cBegin=\"9\" vBegin=\"2\" cEnd=\"9\" vEnd=\"2\" onclick=\"bcv(28,9,2)\">Hos 9:2</ref> (|| <bdbheb>גֹּרֶן</bdbheb>, <bdbheb>יֶקֶב</bdbheb> compare <bdbheb>דָּגָן</bdbheb> v<ref ref=\"Hos 9:1\" b=\"28\" cBegin=\"9\" vBegin=\"1\" cEnd=\"9\" vEnd=\"1\" onclick